{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"This turn corrects an overclaim in the StopSign-resync account. The two source notes about a leader deciding from follower-reported accepted indices and about late Promises not being merged are accurate behavior, but a quorum-intersection check shows neither can by itself explain the run-13 trace: with five nodes and three-node quorums, the accept quorum at index 38 and the leader's prepare quorum must intersect, so a leader that gets 38 chosen must have merged a StopSign-bearing Promise or accepted the StopSign itself at some point. The trace only establishes that leader 4 had no StopSign when it sent node 3's AcceptSync. The update appends a restated interpretation that keeps the executed downstream mechanism and its evidence intact (AcceptSync without a StopSign raises node 3 to accepted 37, the two sequence-expected Decides clamp decided at 37, no PrepareReq is sent, and later resends reuse sequence numbers node 3 already consumed and are ignored) while marking the upstream acquisition of the StopSign as unresolved between the source-consistent paths. The two knowledge uses are softened to source-level alternatives rather than the established cause, and the limitations now state that the receipt does not record which promise or forwarded StopSign gave leader 4 the StopSign or when it accepted it. No execution is requested.\"}"}}
